{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MagnusSumAbsEigBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MagnusSumAbsEigBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.sum_le_sqrt_card_mul_of_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.sum_le_sqrt_card_mul_of_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusSumAbsEigBound.lean#L65-L78","doc":"**The composed bound `(B)`.** Given non-negative `a` (the eigenvalue moduli of `M_λ`) and any\n`F` dominating `Σ aᵢ²` — the role played by Schur's inequality together with\n`‖M_λ‖_F² = tr_λ(X* X)` — we get `Σ aᵢ ≤ √(card ι · F)`. With `F = tr_λ(X* X)` this is exactly\n\n`Σ_i |eig_i(M_λ)| ≤ √(dim_λ · tr_λ(X* X))`,\n\nwhose right-hand side is a positive trace of an algebra element, explicit in the reduced Burau on\nthe hook column (#6556). Hypothesis-carrying by design: Schur's inequality is the classical input\nand is **not** proved here (`_of_` naming per `local/formalizer`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.sum_le_sqrt_card_mul_sum_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.sum_le_sqrt_card_mul_sum_sq","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusSumAbsEigBound.lean#L49-L63","doc":"**Cauchy–Schwarz, in the form the `Σ|eig|` derivation uses.** For non-negative `a`,\n`Σ aᵢ ≤ √(card ι · Σ aᵢ²)`. This is step (i) of the chain: it is what converts control of the\n*squared* moduli (which Schur's inequality supplies, and which the Frobenius norm computes) into\ncontrol of `Σ|eig|` itself. ","signatureChunk":0}]}